1
00:00:05,940 --> 00:00:08,960
YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!

2
00:00:30,340 --> 00:00:31,540
Your moves!

3
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:06,380
If Yu-Gi doesn't show up soon, you
automatically win the duel, sir.

4
00:01:08,620 --> 00:01:09,450
Hmm.

5
00:01:09,533 --> 00:01:11,300
He'd be a fool not to show up.

6
00:01:12,020 --> 00:01:12,850
Mr.

7
00:01:12,933 --> 00:01:15,880
Kaiba, with all due respect,
he only has two minutes.

8
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:21,120
Thanks to Wheeler's little mishap, Yu-Gi's
wasting his time in the medical ward.

9
00:01:21,340 --> 00:01:24,877
But even his pathetic friends
can't keep him away from our duel.

10
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:28,140
For whoever wins faces
Merrick for the championship.

11
00:01:30,360 --> 00:01:34,540
Yugi, we mustn't let Joey's struggle
interfere with our concentration.

12
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:40,160
Remember, in order to overcome
Marek, we must get past Kaiba.

13
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:49,577
Well, well.

14
00:01:49,660 --> 00:01:53,980
Yugi, so, you decided
to show up after all.

15
00:01:54,380 --> 00:01:55,320
Of course.

16
00:01:55,660 --> 00:01:58,657
To miss this duel is to deny my destiny.

17
00:01:58,740 --> 00:02:00,380
Spare me the drama.

18
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:04,280
The second duel of the
semi-finals will now begin!

19
00:02:06,940 --> 00:02:10,400
So, why didn't the Nerd Herd
show up to cheer you on?

20
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:13,913
Are they too busy trying to
wake Wheeler up from his nap?

21
00:02:14,340 --> 00:02:16,920
Joey is in a great deal of danger now.

22
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:18,885
More than you could ever know.

23
00:02:18,980 --> 00:02:21,457
Wheeler shouldn't have been
here in the first place.

24
00:02:21,540 --> 00:02:23,797
I warned him not to
play with the big boys,

25
00:02:23,880 --> 00:02:26,377
and if you ask me, he got
just what he deserved.

26
00:02:26,460 --> 00:02:28,880
A slap in the face by Ra.

27
00:02:29,420 --> 00:02:31,457
And if getting attacked by an Egyptian god

28
00:02:31,540 --> 00:02:34,560
card didn't knock any sense into that kid,

29
00:02:34,780 --> 00:02:35,839
then nothing will.

30
00:02:36,560 --> 00:02:37,820
That's enough, Kaiba!

31
00:02:38,060 --> 00:02:42,825
You have no idea how dangerous this Duel
Monsters tournament of yours has become.

32
00:02:42,920 --> 00:02:46,857
The outcome of the Battle City Finals
could put the whole world at risk.

33
00:02:46,940 --> 00:02:48,720
The only one at risk is you.

34
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:51,900
For once I win, you won't be number one.

35
00:02:52,740 --> 00:02:55,337
Kaiba, it's not always
about being number one.

36
00:02:55,420 --> 00:02:58,500
It's about dueling with
bravery, honor, and respect.

37
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:02,797
And most importantly, putting the
needs of others ahead of your own.

38
00:03:02,880 --> 00:03:07,020
And that's something Joey Wheeler
did every day of his life.

39
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:11,940
The reason he's in that hospital bed is
because he put himself in harm's way.

40
00:03:12,060 --> 00:03:14,340
Just to keep a promise to a friend.

41
00:03:14,780 --> 00:03:15,662
Hmph, pathetic.

42
00:03:15,940 --> 00:03:21,057
Listen, Wheeler can do whatever he wants,
but I'm in this thing for one reason only.

43
00:03:21,140 --> 00:03:23,177
And that's to win the tournament and be

44
00:03:23,260 --> 00:03:26,084
recognized as the greatest
duelist in the world.

45
00:03:26,300 --> 00:03:30,771
So why don't you save your Girl Scout
speech for someone who actually cares?

46
00:03:31,340 --> 00:03:35,987
As far as I'm concerned, Wheeler never
really belonged here in the first place.

47
00:03:40,100 --> 00:03:42,320
Come on, Joey. Keep fighting.

48
00:03:42,720 --> 00:03:44,602
I know you can get through this.

49
00:03:45,580 --> 00:03:46,410
Huh?

50
00:03:46,493 --> 00:03:47,323
Check it out.

51
00:03:47,406 --> 00:03:48,236
It's just a reflex.

52
00:03:48,319 --> 00:03:49,580
He's still out of it.

53
00:03:49,800 --> 00:03:50,640
Come on, Joey.

54
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:54,560
Hey, why isn't that
emergency chopper here yet?

55
00:03:54,760 --> 00:03:56,260
I'm gonna find Mokuba

56
00:03:57,160 --> 00:03:58,800
Hang in there, bro

57
00:03:59,380 --> 00:04:00,340
Poor Joey.

58
00:04:00,760 --> 00:04:03,525
When did this tournament
get so out of control?

59
00:04:04,420 --> 00:04:07,837
The reason I joined the Battle
City tournament was to fulfill a

60
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:11,840
Shizu's prophecy and stop this
great evil from endangering mankind

61
00:04:13,680 --> 00:04:14,960
It's not fair.

62
00:04:15,240 --> 00:04:17,117
Why should my friends
have to suffer just cuz

63
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:19,257
some evil nutcase can't
control his temper?

64
00:04:19,340 --> 00:04:20,980
You look troubled, Taya.

65
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:23,550
Shizu!

66
00:04:23,633 --> 00:04:27,217
I know it seems as though we'll never
be delivered from this darkness,

67
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:29,700
but you must have faith in the light.

68
00:04:30,440 --> 00:04:31,270
Yugi!

69
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:35,500
This is it!

70
00:04:35,680 --> 00:04:37,160
I have to win this duel!

71
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:40,320
For the sake of Joey and the entire world!

72
00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:44,757
Every duel I've fought in this
tournament has led up to this moment.

73
00:04:44,840 --> 00:04:50,420
The moment I finally take down Yugi
Moto and regain my top dueling status.

74
00:04:52,320 --> 00:04:55,177
The last semifinal duel will now begin.

75
00:04:55,260 --> 00:04:58,740
I repeat, this duel
will end the semifinals.

76
00:05:00,100 --> 00:05:01,800
All right, now.

77
00:05:02,220 --> 00:05:03,720
Get ready, Yugi.

78
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:10,200
We're about to find out which one of
our Egyptian god cards reigns supreme.

79
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:13,360
So let the epic battle begin.

80
00:05:15,960 --> 00:05:19,017
The winner of this duel will
advance to the championship

81
00:05:19,100 --> 00:05:22,520
round To face Marek Ishtar
for the Battle City Crown

82
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:28,737
You're about to lose your Egyptian
God card and your reputation And a

83
00:05:28,820 --> 00:05:32,837
duel this momentous deserves an
appropriate setting Wouldn't you agree,

84
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:33,750
Yugi?

85
00:05:33,833 --> 00:05:36,400
Observe the latest in
holographic technology

86
00:05:38,100 --> 00:05:41,041
I think you'll find this
environment quite fitting

87
00:05:46,760 --> 00:05:47,590
Huh?

88
00:05:49,060 --> 00:05:49,890
Explain!

89
00:05:50,160 --> 00:05:53,100
I just want to take you
down in style, Yugi!

90
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:54,580
So observe!

91
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:59,800
Welcome to Duelist Coliseum!

92
00:06:01,100 --> 00:06:02,080
Go, Kyla!

93
00:06:02,260 --> 00:06:04,120
Go, Kyla! Go, Kyla!

94
00:06:04,220 --> 00:06:05,240
Go, Kyla!

95
00:06:07,420 --> 00:06:10,897
Go, Kyla!

96
00:06:10,980 --> 00:06:12,577
to prove who was the strongest.

97
00:06:12,660 --> 00:06:15,597
Now it's our turn to see
which one of us deserves

98
00:06:15,680 --> 00:06:18,320
to call himself the greatest in the world.

99
00:06:18,620 --> 00:06:21,760
So draw your first card
and let the battle begin.

100
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:23,400
With pleasure, Kaiba.

101
00:06:24,080 --> 00:06:26,080
Everything is riding on this duel.

102
00:06:26,380 --> 00:06:28,840
I've got to stay focused and win this.

103
00:06:29,120 --> 00:06:30,240
Here we go.

104
00:06:31,340 --> 00:06:33,320
All right, let's duel.

105
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:35,820
I summon this.

106
00:06:36,900 --> 00:06:38,724
Queen's Knight in defense mode.

107
00:06:40,980 --> 00:06:43,540
Next, I'll place one card face down.

108
00:06:44,220 --> 00:06:45,520
And that's all.

109
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:47,040
Yeah, whatever.

110
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:51,600
I've drawn my Egyptian
God card on my first turn.

111
00:06:51,960 --> 00:06:54,489
Crushing Yugi may be
easier than I thought.

112
00:06:54,860 --> 00:06:57,700
All I have to do is
sacrifice three monsters.

113
00:06:58,340 --> 00:07:01,197
I wonder if Kaiba is
planning to use the same

114
00:07:01,280 --> 00:07:04,420
strategy he used against
a Shizu in his last duel.

115
00:07:04,840 --> 00:07:06,000
Watch this.

116
00:07:06,840 --> 00:07:09,360
Force Raider, attack Herkeldo now!

117
00:07:13,540 --> 00:07:14,370
Ha!

118
00:07:14,453 --> 00:07:16,000
Face-down cards, go!

119
00:07:16,560 --> 00:07:18,740
First up is my Shrink card.

120
00:07:18,960 --> 00:07:21,940
It cuts my Force Raiders'
attack points in half.

121
00:07:24,500 --> 00:07:28,780
This allows my Crush card to
destroy both monsters on the field.

122
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,237
And if that weren't enough,

123
00:07:30,320 --> 00:07:33,980
it also destroys every powerful
monster in your entire deck.

124
00:07:36,400 --> 00:07:39,877
Kaiba may try to destroy my
deck like he did his Shizu's.

125
00:07:39,960 --> 00:07:44,760
But then again, knowing Kaiba, he's got
a whole new strategy planned for me.

126
00:07:45,580 --> 00:07:50,280
And now, I summon my X-Head
Cannon in attack mode.

127
00:07:52,520 --> 00:07:55,020
Next, I'll activate a magic card.

128
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:57,240
Does it look familiar?

129
00:07:57,760 --> 00:07:59,360
It's Spell Sanctuary.

130
00:07:59,680 --> 00:08:04,320
Yes, and it lets us both move one
magic card from our deck to our hand.

131
00:08:04,940 --> 00:08:09,800
So it looks like you were wrong when you
said I never help out anyone but myself,

132
00:08:09,960 --> 00:08:10,790
Yugi.

133
00:08:10,873 --> 00:08:16,120
Now, choose the magic card that I was nice
enough to let you have, so I can move on!

134
00:08:16,560 --> 00:08:17,720
That was weird.

135
00:08:18,060 --> 00:08:22,354
Why would Kaiba want me to have instant
access to my favorite magic card?

136
00:08:22,600 --> 00:08:25,776
Whichever card he chose must
have been worth the risk.

137
00:08:25,980 --> 00:08:29,680
I'll place one card face
down and end my turn.

138
00:08:30,460 --> 00:08:34,380
Before long, Yugi will be
staring into the face of defeat.

139
00:08:35,460 --> 00:08:38,300
Yo, Mokuba, what's up
with the rescue team?

140
00:08:38,540 --> 00:08:39,716
I can't get through.

141
00:08:39,940 --> 00:08:42,417
Something's interfering
with our communications.

142
00:08:42,500 --> 00:08:44,147
We need that helicopter now!

143
00:08:44,700 --> 00:08:47,620
Mayday, this is an emergency. Anyone!

144
00:08:48,020 --> 00:08:49,780
We need medical help now!

145
00:08:50,980 --> 00:08:53,680
Joey, I know you can hear me.

146
00:08:55,700 --> 00:08:57,440
Please don't give up.

147
00:08:57,740 --> 00:09:00,080
Keep fighting, big brother. Huh?

148
00:09:00,300 --> 00:09:01,240
Who said that?

149
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:05,100
And where exactly am I, anyway? Huh?

150
00:09:05,400 --> 00:09:07,080
It's my dueling deck.

151
00:09:08,400 --> 00:09:09,740
Right. That's it.

152
00:09:10,660 --> 00:09:13,380
I'm dreaming about
kicking butt at dulemons.

153
00:09:16,460 --> 00:09:17,660
Poor Joey.

154
00:09:25,600 --> 00:09:29,360
It won't be long before
I control the world.

155
00:09:29,680 --> 00:09:33,180
And the pharaoh bows down before me!

156
00:09:34,920 --> 00:09:37,897
Kaiba! Kaiba! Kaiba! Kaiba!

157
00:09:37,980 --> 00:09:42,120
Soon, I'll give my adoring public
something to really cheer about!

158
00:09:45,620 --> 00:09:47,740
Now, Kaiba, my move!

159
00:09:50,060 --> 00:09:53,354
Kaiba's X-Head Cannon is
stronger than my queen's knife.

160
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:56,461
So why didn't he attack
me when he had the chance?

161
00:09:56,680 --> 00:09:58,597
He must be up to something.

162
00:09:58,680 --> 00:10:03,460
I summon Alpha, the Magnet
Warrior, in defense mode.

163
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:09,820
And then I'll play one
more card, face down.

164
00:10:10,540 --> 00:10:11,700
Your move, Kaiba.

165
00:10:12,300 --> 00:10:16,124
If Yugi thinks he can hide behind
those pathetic monsters of his,

166
00:10:16,260 --> 00:10:19,201
this duel will be over
even sooner than I thought.

167
00:10:20,220 --> 00:10:21,380
Now! Observe!

168
00:10:22,560 --> 00:10:23,390
Excellent.

169
00:10:23,473 --> 00:10:25,760
Everything is falling right into place.

170
00:10:26,580 --> 00:10:31,060
First off, I'll activate this
magic card, Soul Exchange.

171
00:10:31,680 --> 00:10:33,540
That's why you spared my queen.

172
00:10:33,900 --> 00:10:35,120
Very perceptive.

173
00:10:38,140 --> 00:10:43,900
Thanks to my Soul Exchange magic card, both
of your monsters now belong to me, Yugi.

174
00:10:44,280 --> 00:10:46,180
So come forth, my monsters.

175
00:10:47,300 --> 00:10:52,020
Now I can sacrifice them along with
my monster to summon my great beast.

176
00:10:52,420 --> 00:10:54,040
I'm afraid not, Kaiba.

177
00:10:54,560 --> 00:10:56,360
Reveal my face-down card!

178
00:10:56,720 --> 00:10:58,360
Change of heart! No!

179
00:10:58,900 --> 00:11:01,040
Yes, I'm afraid so, Kaiba.

180
00:11:01,420 --> 00:11:04,097
Thanks to my change of
heart magic card's effect,

181
00:11:04,180 --> 00:11:06,945
you no longer have three
monsters to sacrifice.

182
00:11:11,420 --> 00:11:16,200
Now your X-Head Cannon belongs
to me for one turn. Kaiba!

183
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:18,776
You won't summon Obelisk that easily.

184
00:11:18,880 --> 00:11:19,800
Now go!

185
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:22,597
So you've prevented one move.

186
00:11:22,680 --> 00:11:25,800
I've got plenty more
planned, like this one!

187
00:11:26,360 --> 00:11:29,380
Reveal face-down card, Enemy Controller!

188
00:11:31,620 --> 00:11:32,450
What?

189
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:34,953
For the price of a thousand life points,

190
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:38,767
this control pad lets me take
command of one of your monsters!

191
00:11:39,040 --> 00:11:43,680
Enemy Controller, activate
left, right, A, B!

192
00:11:46,440 --> 00:11:47,580
And now,

193
00:11:47,740 --> 00:11:50,817
bring my X-Head Cannon back
to my side of the field

194
00:11:50,900 --> 00:11:54,180
so I have three monsters
to sacrifice once again.

195
00:11:55,120 --> 00:11:57,620
My strategy was foolproof.

196
00:11:59,740 --> 00:12:05,180
I sacrifice Alpha, Queen's
Knight, and X-Head Cannon.

197
00:12:05,600 --> 00:12:07,300
And now...

198
00:12:09,020 --> 00:12:11,897
Obelisk the Tormentor comes...

199
00:12:11,980 --> 00:12:12,862
Hold on, Kaiba!

200
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:14,840
Go, light my sword!

201
00:12:17,280 --> 00:12:18,457
Oh, no!

202
00:12:18,540 --> 00:12:20,180
Oh, yes.

203
00:12:20,580 --> 00:12:25,377
Now your Obelisk the Tormentor is completely
useless to you for three turns, Kaiba,

204
00:12:25,460 --> 00:12:27,284
thanks to my Light Force sword.

205
00:12:27,380 --> 00:12:28,297
What's your rush?

206
00:12:28,380 --> 00:12:30,968
This duel's just getting
interesting, Kaiba.

207
00:12:31,280 --> 00:12:32,980
Why try to end it so soon?

208
00:12:33,500 --> 00:12:36,029
You may have bought
yourself a little time,

209
00:12:36,160 --> 00:12:39,278
but you'll have to face down
Obelisk sooner or later.

210
00:12:42,400 --> 00:12:43,880
Where's Tristan already?

211
00:12:44,220 --> 00:12:46,600
That helicopter better be on its way.

212
00:12:46,840 --> 00:12:49,300
Joey needs help now. You're right.

213
00:12:53,020 --> 00:12:56,317
The evil inside Merrick
must be defeated in

214
00:12:56,400 --> 00:12:59,047
order to reverse the
damage that's been done.

215
00:13:00,560 --> 00:13:04,700
But will the winner of today's
duel be strong enough to stop him?

216
00:13:09,360 --> 00:13:12,240
Your soul exchange card
is no longer in effect,

217
00:13:12,520 --> 00:13:14,677
which means you're not
able to sacrifice my

218
00:13:14,760 --> 00:13:17,617
monsters because you don't
control them anymore.

219
00:13:17,700 --> 00:13:20,300
And Obelisk will have to wait.

220
00:13:23,100 --> 00:13:25,720
I won't be waiting as long as he thinks.

221
00:13:26,140 --> 00:13:27,460
In just three turns,

222
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:32,300
Yugi's life force sword wears off,
and Obelisk returns to my hand.

223
00:13:32,580 --> 00:13:35,404
And by then, I'll have
another way to summon it.

224
00:13:35,640 --> 00:13:37,660
My turn may be over now.

225
00:13:38,160 --> 00:13:40,060
But you're not safe yet.

226
00:13:40,380 --> 00:13:42,140
All right, my move.

227
00:13:43,860 --> 00:13:46,317
So far, I have two monsters on the field.

228
00:13:46,400 --> 00:13:50,920
One more and I'll have enough sacrifices
to summon my Egyptian god card,

229
00:13:51,420 --> 00:13:52,780
Slifer the Sky Dragon!

230
00:13:53,160 --> 00:13:56,631
But first, I have to draw Slifer
from somewhere in my deck.

231
00:13:57,060 --> 00:14:00,472
Anyway, for now I have to deal
with Kaiba's X-Head Cannon.

232
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:04,437
Neither of the monsters I have on the
field are strong enough to take it down.

233
00:14:04,520 --> 00:14:07,497
And nothing in my hand has
that kind of power either.

234
00:14:07,580 --> 00:14:10,120
So, I'll just have to be patient.

235
00:14:10,920 --> 00:14:13,257
Now, I play one card face down.

236
00:14:13,340 --> 00:14:17,760
Then I'll leave both of my monsters
in defense mode and end my turn.

237
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:19,190
Hmph.

238
00:14:19,273 --> 00:14:22,571
I expected more of a challenge
from the top-ranked duelist.

239
00:14:24,240 --> 00:14:29,060
If he keeps playing it safe, my
obelisk will wipe him out in no time.

240
00:14:31,640 --> 00:14:32,920
My move!

241
00:14:38,300 --> 00:14:40,257
This duel should be amusing.

242
00:14:40,340 --> 00:14:45,260
I wonder which of these fools will
summon his Egyptian god card first.

243
00:14:45,560 --> 00:14:47,960
Not that it really matters, of course.

244
00:14:48,660 --> 00:14:49,490
Ha!

245
00:14:49,573 --> 00:14:51,760
Before long, they'll both belong to me.

246
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:55,477
For whoever wins this
battle will be confronting

247
00:14:55,560 --> 00:14:58,720
me in the most treacherous
shadow game ever played.

248
00:14:59,140 --> 00:15:04,300
And then, when the shadows engulf
my opponent, I shall reign supreme.

249
00:15:04,840 --> 00:15:05,740
Ha ha ha ha ha!

250
00:15:07,780 --> 00:15:08,757
Ready, Yugi?

251
